otes": ["Incumbent Tom Cotton (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Tom Cotton seeks a third term in a state that leaned fifteen points Republican at the last presidential election. He enters the final weeks with a large financial edge, roughly five times the cash on hand of challenger Hallie Shoffner, and a Republican get-out-the-vote operation worth about a million dollars. Every major race rating places the contest in the Safe or Solid Republican column.\n\nPolling has been sparse and uneven. Early summer surveys showed single-digit gaps, and one Hendrix College poll even had Shoffner narrowly ahead, but the most recent vote-preference survey from early October gives Cotton an eleven-point lead. Betting markets put his chances around ninety-four percent. A canceled debate and limited outside spending against Cotton point to few signs of a genuine upset threat, though the race has drawn more attention than typical Arkansas Senate contests.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0277, "margin": -11.06}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0629, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0436, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0489, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0435, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.061, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0305, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0524, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0418, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0321, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0276, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0246, "ma